Defects found:

- Line 8: `assert s.count(ANCHOR) == 1` can be removed by optimized Python.
  Exact input: run `python -O scripts/add_f1000_gate.py` when `ssot\make_docx.py` contains zero copies of line 7’s anchor.
  Consequence: line 70 becomes a no-op and line 72 still reports the gate was wired.

- Lines 7, 57-58, 70: the idempotency guard is satisfied by the patch’s own payload because `NEW` still contains the exact `ANCHOR`.
  Exact input: run this script twice against the same `ssot\make_docx.py`.
  Consequence: the F1000 block is inserted repeatedly instead of being a one-time migration.

- Line 4: the script edits a hardcoded `F:` checkout, not necessarily the checkout being run or tested.
  Exact input: run from a `C:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell` mirror while `F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\ssot\make_docx.py` also exists.
  Consequence: the instrument can report success while changing a different copy than the caller intended.

- Line 40: the licence predicate accepts non-equivalent licences by prefix only.
  Exact input: `_ed = {"repository": "Zenodo", "persistent_identifier": "10.x/y", "licence": "CC BY-NC 4.0"}`.
  Consequence: a non-commercial extended-data licence passes a check labelled “CC0 or CC-BY 4.0”.

- Line 44: “OSI-approved licence” is checked as mere truthiness.
  Exact input: `_swx = {"source_code_available_from": "https://x", "archived_source_code_at_time_of_publication": "10.x/y", "licence": "proprietary"}`.
  Consequence: proprietary software passes the OSI-approved licence gate.

- Lines 5 and 71: text-mode read/write does not preserve existing line endings.
  Exact input: `ssot\make_docx.py` stored LF-only on Windows and containing the anchor once.
  Consequence: the script can create an unrelated whole-file CRLF churn diff.

COULD NOT DETERMINE: whether line 45’s `FIG > 0` is PRISMA-flow-specific; missing `ssot\make_docx.py` binding for `FIG`.

No proven merged-cell/off-by-one or negation-dropped defect in this file.
